    "status": "present",
    "value": "A grid holds bricks (1) and empty cells (0). A brick is stable if it is in the top row or is connected, through up, down, left and right neighbours, to a brick in the top row. You receive a sequence of hits; each hit erases the brick at a cell if one is there, after which every brick that is no longer stable falls and disappears. For each hit, return how many bricks fell because of it, not counting the hit brick itself."
  },
